      "side": 1,
      "message": "[error] 🔴 This patch still removes FFmpeg’s `enabled libvpx \u0026\u0026 { ... }` detection block from `configure` globally (not Windows-scoped). That block validates available VP8/VP9 encode/decode components and fails early when `--enable-libvpx` cannot satisfy any supported codec; dropping it can silently mis-detect capabilities and later fail at compile/link/runtime on Linux/macOS/Android. Keep this logic intact and limit Windows-specific workarounds to MSVC-targeted branches only.",
      "revId": "276b67caa259aa3744aad712619b5dab4c7425d9",
      "serverId": "1e26b4c1-6b8c-47ff-9df7-501b633d3b5a"
